12:23.818 --> 12:24.968
Hey.

12:24.970 --> 12:26.919
Whoa! Where were you?

12:26.921 --> 12:29.472
Lance Armstrong's gay
Halloween party?

12:30.975 --> 12:32.875
Very funny.

12:32.877 --> 12:34.010
Wait.

12:34.012 --> 12:36.145
Is that a thing?
Did you get invited?

12:36.147 --> 12:38.298
No. Where were you?

12:38.300 --> 12:40.683
Oh, I was at spin class
with Lyndsey's boyfriend.

12:42.786 --> 12:46.472
Should I ask why or just wait
to see it on &lt;i>48 Hours?&lt;/i>

12:46.474 --> 12:50.643
I simply wanted to find out
what he's got that I don't.

12:50.645 --> 12:55.365
Other than... mental health,
pride and his own underwear?

12:55.367 --> 12:57.834
That's just it.
He does have it all.

12:57.836 --> 13:00.086
I can totally see
why Lyndsey loves him.

13:00.088 --> 13:01.421
He's-he's kind, he's generous,

13:01.423 --> 13:03.923
he's got a smile
that lights up a juice bar.

13:03.925 --> 13:06.876
And-and the kicker is,
he likes me.

13:08.545 --> 13:10.513
And did his smile light up

13:10.515 --> 13:13.433
when you told him
you were plowing his girlfriend?

13:13.435 --> 13:16.969
No. &lt;i>Alan&lt;/i> is plowing
his girlfriend.

13:16.971 --> 13:19.605
Larry's friend, Jeff,
will be joining him

13:19.607 --> 13:22.442
in his luxury box at
the Laker game tomorrow night.

13:22.444 --> 13:24.427
(laughs)

13:24.429 --> 13:26.345
I-I just have to cancel
my plans with Lyndsey.

13:26.347 --> 13:28.314
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

13:28.316 --> 13:31.034
You're telling me you would
rather spend the evening

13:31.036 --> 13:33.403
in &lt;i>Larry's&lt;/i> box?

13:35.322 --> 13:37.740
Hey.
Hey. How'd the acting class go?

13:37.742 --> 13:38.908
It was great.

13:38.910 --> 13:40.126
We did this improv exercise

13:40.128 --> 13:42.045
where I had to pretend
to be high.

13:42.047 --> 13:44.213
I nailed it.

13:44.215 --> 13:46.132
Oh, uh, you know,
in college, uh,

13:46.134 --> 13:47.633
I-I did a little
musical theatre.

13:47.635 --> 13:49.052
And the winner

13:49.054 --> 13:52.138
for the least surprising
sentence ever goes to...

13:52.140 --> 13:54.006
Alan Harper!

13:54.008 --> 13:55.975
Scoff if you will, but, uh,

13:55.977 --> 13:57.560
I actually starred in
our production of &lt;i>Cats.&lt;/i>

13:57.562 --> 14:01.013
And the new winner for least
surprising sentence ever...

14:01.015 --> 14:03.883
Okay, I will have you know
that the campus newspaper said

14:03.885 --> 14:05.551
that my portrayal
of Rum Tum Tugger

14:05.553 --> 14:07.737
was &lt;i>purrfect.&lt;/i>

14:07.739 --> 14:10.356
I've never seen &lt;i>Cats.&lt;/i>

14:10.358 --> 14:11.491
You've never seen...?

14:11.493 --> 14:16.112
♪ The Rum Tum Tugger
is a curious cat. ♪

14:17.364 --> 14:19.332
Well, if you're coming
out of the closet,

14:19.334 --> 14:21.567
come out dancing.

14:21.569 --> 14:23.286
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

14:23.288 --> 14:27.206
Boy, this really makes you
feel like a man, doesn't it?

14:27.208 --> 14:31.627
Basketball, cheerleaders,
a crisp Pinot Noir.

14:31.629 --> 14:33.596
There's beer in the fridge, too.

14:33.598 --> 14:35.965
What? And undo all
that spinning? Oh, no.

14:35.967 --> 14:38.384
A second on the lips,
a month on the hips.

14:38.386 --> 14:39.602
(laughs)

14:39.604 --> 14:41.921
Did you ever do this
gay character in your stand-up?

14:41.923 --> 14:45.942
Yeah. It was a real
crowd-pleaser.

14:45.944 --> 14:48.778
I, uh... I also do a-a
character who's really cheap.

14:48.780 --> 14:51.764
(laughs) "Hey, is everything here
free? Even those shrimp""

14:51.766 --> 14:53.098
Nice.

14:53.100 --> 14:55.618
If I kept going,
I'd say, "Hey, uh,

14:55.620 --> 14:57.787
can I get a to-go container?"

14:57.789 --> 14:59.822
Help yourself, you cheap queer.

14:59.824 --> 15:01.991
(laughs)

15:04.044 --> 15:06.546
Hey, uh, can I get
a to-go container?

15:15.672 --> 15:17.557
(laughs)

15:17.559 --> 15:21.177
Hope we don't end up
on the Kiss Cam.

15:23.296 --> 15:26.098
I've been told
my kisses are like French fries.

15:26.100 --> 15:27.633
Can't stop with just one.

15:27.635 --> 15:29.068
(laughs)

15:32.656 --> 15:34.991
LARRY: Lyndsey, what
a surprise!

15:35.826 --> 15:37.810
Lyndsey?

15:37.812 --> 15:39.278
Hey, sweetie.
My plans fell through.

15:39.280 --> 15:40.830
Well, now you
can meet Jeff.

15:40.832 --> 15:43.148
Jeff, this is my
girlfriend Lyndsey.

15:44.768 --> 15:47.152
He's always joking
around. Get over here!

15:51.425 --> 15:53.125
Hi.

15:53.127 --> 15:55.711
Hi. So, this is the guy

15:55.713 --> 15:57.496
you were telling me about?

15:57.498 --> 15:59.799
Yes, uh, uh, Lyndsey, was it?

15:59.801 --> 16:01.684
Uh-huh.

16:02.853 --> 16:04.887
I'm sorry.
I didn't catch your name.

16:04.889 --> 16:07.773
This is Jeff.
Jeff Strongman.

16:12.029 --> 16:15.531
Strongman?
That's uniqu aname.

16:15.533 --> 16:17.283
Uh, it's-it's German.

16:17.285 --> 16:19.735
Uh, it's actually pronounced
Strungmin.

16:19.737 --> 16:20.953
(clears throat)

16:20.955 --> 16:24.189
Strungmin?
Mmm.

16:24.191 --> 16:26.525
It almost sounds
made up, doesn't it?

16:26.527 --> 16:29.295
Yeah, well, it's not,
so shut up.

16:33.000 --> 16:34.217
Sweetie, it-it's cold in here.

16:34.219 --> 16:37.036
I think I left a jacket
in the car. Would you mind?

16:37.038 --> 16:38.871
Of course.
(laughs)

16:38.873 --> 16:41.724
Hey, I can trust you alone
with my girlfriend, right?

16:41.726 --> 16:46.262
If you can't, then my name's not
Jeff Strungmin.

16:49.600 --> 16:51.400
(door closes)

16:51.402 --> 16:52.902
What the hell is
going on, Jeff?

16:52.904 --> 16:54.987
Are you trying to
break me and Larry up?

16:54.989 --> 16:57.356
No, I would never
do that to Larry.

16:57.358 --> 16:59.892
Then what are
you doing here?

16:59.894 --> 17:02.445
I just... I wanted to figure out
what Larry has that I don't

17:02.447 --> 17:03.863
so that I could be
more like him,

17:03.865 --> 17:05.081
and then you'd come
back to me.

17:05.083 --> 17:07.116
Look, I already
have a Larry.

17:07.118 --> 17:10.036
If you turned into Larry,
I'd have to find another Alan.

17:10.038 --> 17:11.904
Really?
Yes, you idiot!

17:11.906 --> 17:13.172
Don't you get it?

17:13.174 --> 17:15.758
No man has ever turned
me on like you do.

17:15.760 --> 17:19.095
It's a gift and a curse.

17:19.097 --> 17:21.297
Shut up.

17:21.299 --> 17:23.633
I'll stop talking,
but I won't stop...

17:23.635 --> 17:25.701
(imitates buzzing)
No, stop it.

17:25.703 --> 17:26.852
(imitates buzzg)

17:26.854 --> 17:28.204
I'm still mad at you!

17:28.206 --> 17:29.372
Well, I don't blame you.

17:29.374 --> 17:30.589
I have been very naughty.

17:30.591 --> 17:32.642
Perhaps I should be punished.

17:32.644 --> 17:34.226
Let's go.

17:34.228 --> 17:35.278
What...? Wait. Where?

17:35.280 --> 17:36.729
We'll do it in
the bathroom.

17:36.731 --> 17:37.897
Seriously?
Oh, yeah.

17:37.899 --> 17:39.899
Beats the hell
out of the Kiss Cam.

17:42.653 --> 17:44.787
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

17:44.789 --> 17:46.322
Hey.

17:46.324 --> 17:47.490
Hey.

17:47.492 --> 17:48.958
How did the acting class go?

17:48.960 --> 17:50.293
I didn't go.

17:50.295 --> 17:51.744
(loudly):
Liar!

17:51.746 --> 17:55.331
I talked to my friend,
and he said you &lt;i>didn't&lt;/i> go,

17:55.333 --> 17:57.550
so admit it!

17:58.385 --> 18:00.586
I just did.

18:00.588 --> 18:02.054
I know!

18:02.056 --> 18:05.141
And I wasn't prepared for that.

18:05.143 --> 18:08.311
I went to the first class,
but it was lame.

18:08.313 --> 18:11.296
It doesn't meant that you're not
gonna learn something from it.

18:11.298 --> 18:14.466
Do you think that I just said,
"Oh, I have a software idea

18:14.468 --> 18:17.153
and I'm gonna sell it for
a billion dollars the next day"?

18:17.155 --> 18:20.323
I Googled you.
That is what happened.

18:20.325 --> 18:22.641
The point is, is that,
if-if that hadn't happened,

18:22.643 --> 18:24.977
I would have been willing
to work for it.

18:24.979 --> 18:26.445
Look, I-I get it,

18:26.447 --> 18:29.248
but all this touchy-feely stuff
just freaks me out.

18:29.250 --> 18:31.617
Half the reason
I got into acting

18:31.619 --> 18:33.619
was so I could pretend
to be someone else,

18:33.621 --> 18:35.588
not so I could spend time
thinking about

18:35.590 --> 18:37.757
how I don't
get along with my mom.

18:38.608 --> 18:40.259
And how I never knew my father.

18:40.261 --> 18:41.761
How I'm 25 years old

18:41.763 --> 18:45.348
and living in the guest room
of a stranger's house.

18:45.350 --> 18:46.966
(sighs)

18:46.968 --> 18:48.968
I'm sorry.

18:48.970 --> 18:52.004
I didn't mean
to stir all this up. I just...

18:52.006 --> 18:55.358
And that's why
I don't need acting lessons.

18:58.445 --> 19:00.196
You know what?

19:00.981 --> 19:02.148
If you don't want

19:02.150 --> 19:05.735
to help yourself,
I can't force you.

19:06.570 --> 19:08.654
But the choices
that you make today

19:08.656 --> 19:11.690
are going to affect you
for the rest of your life.

19:11.692 --> 19:14.193
And as long as you live
under my roof...

19:14.195 --> 19:15.878
Oh, God, kill me.

19:17.013 --> 19:18.998
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

19:19.000 --> 19:20.299
(moaning)

19:20.301 --> 19:22.785
Is everything okay?
Yeah.

19:22.787 --> 19:24.303
The only thing
I can feel in your pants

19:24.305 --> 19:25.421
is the shrimp that you stole.

19:25.423 --> 19:27.473
I'm sorry. I'm-I'm
just nervous.

19:27.475 --> 19:29.258
Can you do this or not?

19:29.260 --> 19:30.526
I don't think so.

19:30.528 --> 19:32.311
I mean, what would Larry say?

19:32.313 --> 19:34.980
LARRY:
&lt;i>Come on, Jeff. Don't quit.&lt;/i>

19:36.016 --> 19:37.850
What?

19:37.852 --> 19:39.218
I didn't say anything.

19:39.220 --> 19:40.986
LARRY:
&lt;i>You can do it.&lt;/i>

19:40.988 --> 19:42.554
&lt;i>Yes, you can.&lt;/i>

19:42.556 --> 19:45.224
You know what?
Maybe I can do this.

19:45.226 --> 19:46.242
Really?

19:46.244 --> 19:47.660
LARRY:
&lt;i>Attaboy.&lt;/i>

19:47.662 --> 19:49.328
&lt;i>Don't go soft on me.&lt;/i>

19:49.330 --> 19:51.363
&lt;i>Go, Jeff, go.&lt;/i>

19:51.365 --> 19:53.082
Oh, Alan.

19:53.084 --> 19:54.200
Call me Jeff.

19:54.202 --> 20:01.240
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:03.050 --> 20:05.351
[♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:07.104 --> 20:09.372
Guess who got an audition.

20:09.374 --> 20:10.356
Really?

20:10.358 --> 20:11.641
Yep.

20:11.643 --> 20:13.643
That's amazing.
Tell me about it.

20:13.645 --> 20:16.479
Well, I went back
to the acting class.

20:16.481 --> 20:17.763
(chuckles)

20:17.765 --> 20:19.365
Isn't that funny?

20:20.267 --> 20:22.285
The thing I suggested you do

20:22.287 --> 20:24.254
that you didn't want to do

20:24.256 --> 20:27.340
turned out to be the exact thing
that you should have done.

20:27.342 --> 20:30.543
Yeah, well, after about an hour
of that acting crap,

20:30.545 --> 20:31.961
I had to go get a drink.

20:31.963 --> 20:34.113
So, I bailed
and went to a bar

20:34.115 --> 20:35.582
where I met a casting director.

20:35.584 --> 20:38.784
Turned out she was a lesbian,
so I had a leg up.

20:40.020 --> 20:42.255
And when I put it down,
I had an audition.

20:43.807 --> 20:46.009
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:46.011 --> 20:48.511
Oh.

20:50.598 --> 20:52.798
You have got to stop doing that.

20:52.800 --> 20:56.169
And you have to stop looking
so pretty when you sleep.

20:56.171 --> 20:58.238
Okay, I heard it that
time. It was creepy.

20:58.240 --> 21:00.823
You know what? I don't have
to go anywhere today.

21:00.825 --> 21:01.870
Really?
Yeah.

21:01.895 --> 21:03.895
Larry's got a friend
picking him up at the airport.

21:04.920 --> 21:07.004
Oh, shoot!
Shoot! Shoot!

21:07.006 --> 21:12.006
